{
  "total_prepetition_claim": 125000,
  "admin_503b9": {
    "amount": 78100,
    "invoices": ["MS-7788", "MS-7815"]
  },
  "general_unsecured": 46900,
  "reclamation": {
    "available": false,
    "why": "Technically still exercisable but practically worthless, so not relied on. Under 11 U.S.C. Sec. 546(c)(1) (library: bc_503b9_546c.md), goods received within 45 days pre-petition (on/after 2026-01-24: MS-7740, MS-7788, MS-7815) may be reclaimed only by written demand not later than 45 days after receipt or 20 days after the petition (2026-03-30) where the 45 days expire post-commencement; no such written reclamation demand has been made (the 2026-03-12 letter demanded payment, not return of goods), and the window for the earliest goods (received 2026-02-04) closes imminently. Decisively, the library states reclamation is subject to prior liens - here the DIP lender's blanket lien - so reclamation would recover nothing. The same MS-7788/MS-7815 goods are already captured by the Sec. 503(b)(9) administrative claim, which is the effective route. Assumption: Mesa holds no purchase-money security interest and the goods remain identifiable in debtor possession."
  },
  "bar_date": "2026-06-11",
  "preference": {
    "transfers_in_90_days": 180000,
    "ordinary_course_defense": {
      "protected": 95000,
      "exposed": 85000,
      "reasoning": "Petition 2026-03-10; 90-day window opens 2025-12-10 (11 U.S.C. Sec. 547(b)(4), (f); library: bc_547.md). Four payments fall inside: 2025-12-18 $51,000 (45 days after invoice, ACH), 2026-01-22 $44,000 (43 days, ACH), 2026-02-10 $48,200 (29 days, ACH), 2026-02-27 $36,800 (25 days, WIRE demanded by Mesa). Protected (Sec. 547(c)(2)(A)): the 12/18 and 1/22 payments (=$95,000) match the parties' 12-month history of 43-47 day ACH payments on a regular cadence. Exposed (= $85,000): the 2/10 payment (29 days - well outside the 43-47 day history, arriving after Mesa's unilateral 2026-01-20 shortening of terms to NET 15, and the library states payments under shortened terms generally fall outside (c)(2)(A)) and the 2/27 partial payment (25 days, wire on demand - the library expressly names 'wire on demand' under 'pressure' as outside (c)(2)(A)). Sec. 547(c)(2)(B) (ordinary industry terms) could protect the 2/10 payment but we have no industry payment-terms evidence yet - see QUESTIONS.md. Burden on these defenses is Mesa's (Sec. 547(g))."
    },
    "new_value_defense": 85000,
    "net_exposure_estimate": 0
  },
  "stay_violations": [
    "2026-03-12: 'FINAL NOTICE - pay $210,000 within 5 days or we refer to collections' letter, mailed and emailed 2 days post-petition - an act to collect a pre-petition claim, 11 U.S.C. Sec. 362(a)(6) (library: bc_362.md: 'Dunning letters ... after the petition are acts to collect').",
    "2026-03-15: collection call to Redwood AP demanding payment - a collection call post-petition, Sec. 362(a)(6).",
    "2026-03-18: email to Redwood CFO threatening to 'hold all future shipments and report to credit bureaus' - the credit-bureau threat is expressly an act to collect per the library, Sec. 362(a)(6); the shipment-withholding threat is collection leverage and compounds the willfulness risk."
  ],
  "immediate_actions": [
    "STOP all collection activity against Redwood today: no calls, letters, emails, credit-bureau reports, or shipment-withholding threats tied to the pre-petition debt; put the AR team's standing 'keep collecting' instruction in writing to a stop. Repeat violations risk willful-violation liability under Sec. 362(k) (actual damages, attorneys' fees, possible punitive damages).",
    "Have counsel send a short corrective communication to debtor's counsel confirming Mesa will abide by the stay, and preserve all collection records; do not send further demand letters.",
    "Prepare Official Form 410 proof of claim for $125,000 to be filed well before the 2026-06-11 bar date (Fed. R. Bankr. P. 3002(c), 3003(c); library: frbp_3002_3003.md) - late claims barred absent excusable neglect.",
    "Assert the $78,100 Sec. 503(b)(9) administrative portion separately, by motion or the procedure the bar-date order specifies (library: frbp_3002_3003.md).",
    "Calendar 2026-03-30 as the outside date for a written Sec. 546(c) reclamation demand, but treat it as a negotiating lever only - it is gutted by the DIP lender's blanket lien (library: bc_503b9_546c.md).",
    "Contact debtor's counsel before the 2026-04-02 critical-vendor hearing on Dkt. 44 if Mesa wants consideration as a critical vendor; be ready to agree to customary trade terms during the case (library: critical_vendor_practice.md).",
    "Quantify and reserve for preference exposure ($180,000 received in the window; realistic residual near $0 after defenses, see preference block), gather industry payment-terms evidence for Sec. 547(c)(2)(B), and remember Sec. 502(d): the court can disallow Mesa's claim until any preference liability is paid (library: bc_502d_setoff.md)."
  ]
}

